 "title": "Appraiser | Pawnee County, KS",
 "text": "Appraiser | Pawnee County, KS\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nGovernment\nBusiness\nVisitors\nElections\nI Want To...\nSearch\nAppraiser\nParcel Search\nPawnee County GIS & Registered Parcel Search\nProperty Search - Appraiser Portal (Taxes)\nORKA\nMarket Study\nRESULTS OF THE 2026 MARKET STUDY.pdf\n2026 vs 2025 Ag Use Values.pdf\nThe Pawnee County Appraiser’s Office will begin our annual reinspection of real estate properties, this process will continue throughout the summer and into the fall. The Pawnee County Appraiser’s Office is mandated by K.S.A. 79-1476 to re-inspect all real property in Pawnee County every six years. The purpose of this inspection is to verify that our data is current and represents the property accurately.\nThis year we will be working in the townships of Ash Valley , Lincoln , Orange , Shiley , Valley Center & Walnut .\nPawnee County Appraiser’s Office personnel can be identified by Pawnee County photo identification badges and will be driving a vehicle marked with the Pawnee County logo.\nOther routine work will continue throughout Pawnee County, such as reviewing recent sale properties, permits and parcels with new or demolished buildings. Property owners with questions may contact the Pawnee County Appraiser’s Office at 620-285-2915.\nContact The County Appraiser\nThis form has been modified since it was saved. Please review all fields before submitting.\n* indicates a required field\nName *\nEmail Address * In order for us to contact you, please fill in your email.\nAddress *\nCity\nState\nZip Code\nPhone Number *\nFax Number\nQuestions / Comments Please ask any questions you have and we will get back to you as soon as possible. Thank You!.\nLe ave T his Bla nk:\nReceive an email copy of this form.\nEmail address\nThis field is not part of the form submission.\nSubmit\nOK\nAppeals\nGuide to Property Valuation Equalization Appeals\nGuide to Property Valuation Payment Under Protest Appeals\nPayment Under Protest Form\nNeighborhood Revitalization\nPN Neighborhood Revitalization 2026 Plan\nNRP Brochure 2026\nQuick Links\nKansas Board of Tax Appeals\nKansas Department of Revenue - Division of Property Valuation\n2026 Oil & Gas Guide\n2026 Personal Property Guide\nProperty Tax Calendar\nView All\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nContact Us\nTina Keeler, RMA\nCounty Appraiser\nEmail\nPhone: 620-285-2915\nAppraiser\nNeighborhood Revitalization\nAttorney\nCommunity Corrections\nCounty Clerk\nHomestead FAQs\nCounty Extension\nEmergency Management\nPrescribed Burn Association\nVolunteers\nHealth Department\nFor Children\nImmunizations\nServices\nMaternal & Infant Program (M&I)\nPreventive Services\nSexually Transmitted Infection Clinic\nWomen, Infants, & Children (WIC)\nWomen’s Health Clinic\nWIC Application Page\nHealth Dept Job Application Page\nHumane Society\nLibrary\nRegister of Deeds\nRoad & Bridge / Noxious Weed / Zoning\nRoad & Bridge Department Job Application Page\nRight of Way Wrongs\nSheriff\nJail Information\nQuick Links\nSolid Waste\nLandfill Employment Page\nTreasurer\nTreasurers Job Application Page\nEMS\nCourthouse Custodial\nNeighborhood Revitalization\nAgendas & Minutes\nEmployment\nParcel Search\nAlerts & Notifications\nGrow\nCares\nConnects\nexplore\nContact Us\nPawnee County Courthouse\n715 Broadway\nLarned, KS 67550\nPhone: 620-285-3721\nPopular Links\nPublic Transportation Bus\nLocal Landmarks\nJobs\nGuide to Voting\nCounty Commission\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Maps\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×",
